########## Part B: named volume. Data lives outside the container

=== 14. Create a volume
$ docker volume create vitals-data
vitals-data
-> ok

=== 15. List volumes
$ docker volume ls --filter name=vitals-data
DRIVER    VOLUME NAME
local     vitals-data
-> ok

=== 16. Save a reading into the volume
$ docker run --rm -v vitals-data:/data vitals-logger P-001 120 80 72
Saved reading for P-001
File: /data/readings.csv
Readings in file: 1
-> ok

=== 17. Another container, same volume. The count goes up
